---
description: Grey 3D scene to the same scene textured from several calibrated views of one generated multi-view sheet: verified passes, one multi-reference edit, consistency score, visibility-aware UV fusion, diagnostic and PBR .blend
globs: **/*.py
alwaysApply: false
---

Copy this file into your project's `.cursor/rules/`. Install the skill too (Cursor reads `~/.cursor/skills`,
`~/.claude/skills` and `.agents/skills`), so the rule can point at it.

- Use the `multiview-blockout-to-real` skill: scaffold a case with `scripts/mvb2r.py new`, write `case.json`
  yourself, check the camera coverage table and the pass verification before any paid call, then `run CASE --to
  targets`, look, and continue.
- Accept refined views only by the thresholds written in the case's `CONTRACT.md` before looking.
- Choose the fusion method by leave-one-view-out and seam visibility, never by source-view reproduction.
- Nothing generated is composited into a render. A failed stage stops. A resize is a resize.
- The reviewer is a fresh session that sees only its images.
- Report the consistency table, coverage per object, the residual baked shading and the call count with cost
  "unknown" when the price is a placeholder.
